            <ArticleTitle>Quantitative analysis of nitroglycerin-induced coronary artery vasodilation in transplanted hearts.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>886-91</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Quantitative serial coronary angiograms performed annually over a 3-year period after transplantation in 26 orthotopic heart transplant recipients showed persistently normal nitroglycerin-induced vasodilation. The vasodilator response to nitroglycerin did not predict development of graft arteriopathy; the presence of graft arteriopathy did not prevent a substantial vasodilator response to nitroglycerin.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
